aces of F n . We see that |G(k, n)| = m(k, n) = (pn − 1)(p n − p)(p n − p 2 ) · · ·(p n p k − 1) (p k − 1)(p k − p)(p k − p 2 ) · · ·(p k − p k−1 ) . A universal cycle of the k-subspaces is a circular arrangement of m(k, n) elements of F n , C = v1v2v3 . . .v m(k,n), such that every k-subspace of G(k, n) has exactly one basis that is a block of k consecutive elements of C.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOn Universal Cycles for k-Subsets of an n-Set | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/2414517_On_Universal_Cycles_for_k-Subsets_of_an_n-Set)\nciteturn7search9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; Hurlbert ... Image: Request Full-text Paper PDF ... To read the full-text of this research, you can request a copy directly from the author. ... We will let the partition size vector (PSV) of an edge be a k-tuple that expresses the number of 1's, 2's, etc. in order.\n\nArticle\n\n# On Universal Cycles for k-Subsets of an n-Set\n\n  * October 2000\n  * SIAM Journal on Discrete Mathematics 7(4):598-604\n\nDOI:10.1137/S0895480191220861\n\nAuthors:\n\nG. H. Hurlbert\n\n  * Arizona State University\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research, you can request a copy directly from the author.\n\n## Abstract\n\nA Universal Cycle, or Ucycle, for k-subsets of [n] = f1; : : : ; ng is a cyclic sequence of n k integers with the property that each subset of [n] of size k appears exactly once consecutively in the sequence. Chung, Diaconis, and Graham have conjectured their existence for xed k and large n when nj n k . Here we exhibit Ucycles for k = 3; 4; 6 and large n relatively prime to k.\n\n\n## No full-text available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the full-text of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the author.\n\nRequest full-text PDF\n\n## Citations (43)\n-------------------------------------------------------------